course: dictionary
lesson: 15259
title: Shrieking: loud, high and sharp
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shrieking means making a loud, high, sharp cry. People shriek when they are scared, hurt, excited or laughing hard. «The children were shrieking with laughter on the water slide.» The words «with laughter» tell you the shrieks are happy, not hurt.
explain: The words around shrieking give you the clues. «The girl saw a spider and started shrieking.» A spider can make people feel frightened, so here shrieking shows fear. Ask yourself: why is this person making a sound this loud?
explain: Shrieking can also describe things that are not people. «The shrieking wind rattled the windows all night.» The wind makes a loud, high, sharp sound, so the word fits. Shrieking can also be a noun: «The shrieking in the playground grew louder.» Here it means the sound of loud high cries.
fact: Shriek is a verb. Its forms are shriek, shrieks, shrieked and shrieking.
fact: «Shrieking» can be an adjective, a verb or a noun, depending on the sentence.
fact: «Shrieking» means making a loud, high, sharp cry, from fear, pain, excitement or laughter.
fact: Shrieking with laughter means laughing very loudly and happily.
fact: Shrieking in terror means crying out loudly because you are very scared.
exercise: «The children were shrieking with laughter in the water fight.» What does shrieking mean here? | *Making loud, high cries of fun | Whispering secrets | Walking slowly home | Sleeping quietly in the sun
exercise: «She saw a spider and started shrieking.» Why might she be shrieking? | *She is frightened | She has finished her lunch | She is very tired and sleepy | She is reading a quiet book
exercise: «The shrieking in the playground grew louder.» In this sentence, shrieking is a noun. What does it mean? | A kind of bird's nest | A small quiet whisper | *The sound of loud high cries | A type of hat
test: «The shrieking wind rattled the windows all night.» What does shrieking tell you about the wind? | *It made a loud, high, sharp sound | It was warm and sunny | It was soft and gentle | It stopped quickly
test: «She shrieked when the cold water splashed her.» Which word means nearly the same as shrieked here? | *Screamed | Smiled | Whispered | Yawned
exam: «Tom heard shrieking coming from the attic.» What do the words around shrieking tell you? | It was the sound of a book being closed | *Someone was making a loud, high cry, perhaps from fear | It was a quiet sound from a sleeping cat | Nobody was in the house
